## Where the index comes from (build-time)

### Harvester tool

Tool project:
- `.tools/Bible.Alarm.AudioLinksHarvestor/Program.cs`

It builds an index artifact at:
- `.tools/_index/index.zip` (see `.tools/Bible.Alarm.AudioLinksHarvestor/Utility/DirectoryHelper.cs`)

The MAUI app embeds that zip as an embedded resource:
- `src/Bible.Alarm/Bible.Alarm.csproj` embeds `..\..\.tools\_index\index.zip` as `Resources\index.zip`

### Harvester phases (important mental model)

The harvester runs in two big phases:

1) **DISCOVERY**
   - uses JW APIs to discover which languages exist for each publication/section
   - writes to in-memory stores, then later seeds “discovery tables”:
     - `PublicationLanguages`
     - `SectionLanguages`

2) **HARVESTING + SEEDING**
   - downloads/constructs the actual publication/section/track records that the app uses
   - seeds **English (“E”) by default**
   - seeds “no-language” melody music (e.g. `iam`) separately
   - zips the resulting SQLite DB into `index.zip`

---

## Harvest types (three modes)

Enum:
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Models/Enums/HarvestType.cs`

### 1) Flat

- publications: most **vocal music**, **video**
- shape: Publication → Tracks
- API: `GETPUBMEDIALINKS` with `track=` or equivalent flat listing

### 2) Sectioned

- publications: **Bible** (books/parts), **melody music** (e.g. `iam` discs/sections)
- shape: Publication → Sections → Tracks
- API: `GETPUBMEDIALINKS` with section selection, but the **param differs by type**:
  - Bible-style: `pub={publicationCode}&booknum={sectionCode}`
  - Melody disc-style (e.g. `iam-9`): `pub={sectionCode}` (no `booknum`)

### 3) MediatorSectioned

- publications: **dramas**
- shape: Publication → Sections (discovered dynamically) → Tracks
- APIs:
  - Mediator API for discovery: `https://app.jw-cdn.org/apis/mediator/v1/...`
  - then `GETPUBMEDIALINKS` for the actual track links for each discovered section code

