## APIs used (and what for)

### GETPUBMEDIALINKS (primary)

Constant:
- `AppConstants.ApiEndpoints.JwOrgIndexServiceBaseUrl = "https://b.jw-cdn.org/apis/pub-media/GETPUBMEDIALINKS"`

Used for:
- Bible audio links
- vocal music links
- melody music links
- video links
- drama links (after section discovery)

Common query params (varies by harvest type):
- `output=json`
- `pub={publicationCode}`
- `fileformat=mp3|mp4`
- `langwritten={LanguageCode}` (e.g. `E`)
- `alllangs=1` during discovery
- section selection for sectioned publications:
  - Bible: `booknum={sectionCode}`
  - Melody discs (e.g. `iam-9`): `pub={sectionCode}` (disc code becomes the pub)

### Mediator API (category discovery)

Constant:
- `AppConstants.ApiEndpoints.JwOrgMediatorApiBaseUrl = "https://app.jw-cdn.org/apis/mediator/v1"`

Used mainly for:
- drama section discovery (and in some cases localized metadata)

### Languages list (seed language table)

Harvester seeds the full language list using the JW site language endpoint:
- implemented in `.tools/Bible.Alarm.AudioLinksHarvestor/Seeders/LanguageSeeder.cs` (called from `DbSeeder`)

---

## How the app gets the index at runtime

On first run (or if missing), the app extracts the embedded resource:
- `src/Bible.Alarm/Services/Media/MediaIndexService.cs`
  - copies embedded `index.zip` into storage root
  - extracts to produce `mediaIndex.db`
  - writes a version stamp via `IMediaIndexVersionService`

Notes:
- The code currently assumes the media index is updated by **app updates**, not by downloading a new index from the network (see comments in `MediaIndexService`).

